Hello,<br />
Thank you for yur interest in hosting a blood drive at LA Fitness.&nbsp;It would be a priviledge to help you.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
The first two steps are simple.
<ol>
	<li style="margin-left:0in;">Secure a location inside with a minimum of 1200 sq feet.
	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha;">
		<li style="margin-left:0in;">We can bring a bus to a location, but this <i>limits</i> dates available and how many people we can process.&nbsp; It also doesn&rsquo;t give you that &ldquo;community&rdquo; experience so many donors are expecting.</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
	<li style="margin-left:0in;">Create a social media event or survey monkey to see how much interest there is in hosting a drive.&nbsp;
	<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha;">
		<li style="margin-left:0in;">A simple statement of &ldquo;We are thinking of hosting a lifesaving blood drive this Fall, would you be available to donate? Y/N&rdquo; is sufficient.</li>
		<li style="margin-left:0in;">These soft pledges tell us what % of patients we can serve, &nbsp;how many people to expect and how much equipment we will need.</li>
		<li style="margin-left:0in;">These soft pledges can help fill the appointment slots, when it&rsquo;s time.</li>
	</ol>
	</li>
</ol>
<span style="font-family:times new roman,serif;"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;">&nbsp;<br />
Once we have that information we can look at dates and times to hold your drive.&nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Have a date in mind? We book drives on a first come first serve basis and would like to be able to accommodate all requests, but it is not always possible. We always need blood and hope that you are always willing to give.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to reach out to me.<br />
<br />
Thank you in advance,</span></span><br />
